<title>USA: Michigan unemployment rate dips to 4.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Michigan unemployment rate dips to 4.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michigan's unemployment rate dropped to a seasonally adjusted record low rate of 4.3 percent for March, the state's employment security agency reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>The agency had reported a jobless rate of 4.5 percent in February and 5.1 percent for March 1996.</p>
<p>Service sector and retail jobs increased in March, while the auto industry and government sectors reported scattered job losses, the agency reported.</p>
<p>((--David Bailey, 312-408-8647))</p>
